{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Thus</b> — Rabbi Moses said: יוצר is like חבור, and like it, in his view, [is] יוצר עמל עלי חוק (Psalms 94:20). But the correct [interpretation]: that it is according to its plain meaning." "<b>And the locusts</b> — The Aramaic translation [of] ארבה." "<b>And behold</b> — He saw that HaShem was forming locusts." "<b>The latter growth</b> — The grass that grows after the latter rain comes down, and behold the לקש is cut for the king's livestock, before the reed grows."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The verse cited is Psalms 94:20; Ibn Ezra quotes it to illustrate Rabbi Moses's proposed reading of יוצר as 'joining/banding' rather than 'forming'.", 3 "Reading עלות הקנה ('growth of the reed'); some witnesses may read differently, but the sense follows the parallel passage in Ibn Ezra's commentary on similar agricultural terms."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:18:26.451550686Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}